-- title:
--   Divisibility of [P-Q] modulo n on a curve
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $0$ and let $F$ be a field which is a $K$-algebra, subject to the finite-generation hypothesis `hfg`: some $x \in F$ is transcendental over $K$ and $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$. Assume `IsCurveOver K F`, i.e. every nonzero $f \in F$ has a finitely supported divisor of degree $0$ whose value at each place is $\operatorname{ord}_v f$, every place has residue field finite over $K$, and the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega[F/K]$ is free of rank $1$ over $F$. Here a place $v$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing $\operatorname{im}(K \to F)$, proper in $F$ and a principal ideal ring, and $\operatorname{ord}_v f$ is minus the logarithm of its $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation at $f$. Let $n$ be a nonzero natural number and $P, Q$ two places. Then there exists $f \in F$, $f \neq 0$, such that for every place $v$ the integer $n$ divides $\operatorname{ord}_v f - (\delta_P - \delta_Q)(v)$, where $\delta_P - \delta_Q$ is the divisor $\mathrm{Finsupp.single}\ P\ 1 - \mathrm{Finsupp.single}\ Q\ 1$.
--
--   This is the divisibility of the class $[P-Q]$ in the degree-zero divisor class group of the curve with function field $F$, in the concrete form 'some rational function has divisor congruent to $P-Q$ modulo $n$'; classically it follows from surjectivity of multiplication by $n$ on the $K$-points of the Jacobian. It is the generator-level input to [`AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.exists_nsmul_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.exists_nsmul_eq), the divisibility of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$, and is proved by descending to a countable model, extending the constant field to $\mathbb{C}$ and invoking the complex case.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_exists_natCast_dvd_ord_sub_single_sub_single.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open AlgebraicCurve

theorem AlgebraicCurve.Place.exists_natCast_dvd_ord_sub_single_sub_single (K F : Type*) [Field K]
    [Field F] [Algebra K F] [IsAlgClosed K] [CharZero K]
    (hfg : ∃ x : F, Transcendental K x ∧ FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({x} : Set F)) F)
    [IsCurveOver K F]
    (n : ℕ) (hn : n ≠ 0) (P Q : Place K F) :
    ∃ f : F, f ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ v : Place K F,
      (n : ℤ) ∣ v.ord f - (Finsupp.single P 1 - Finsupp.single Q 1 : Divisor K F) v := by sorry
